# NET-MESH-0 pass 1: the DesertServer target on macOS (Docs/contracts/NET-ARCH.md §6, §9 row NET-MESH-0).
# Outside the editor (DesertEngine-scratch/NET-MESH-0/; the world is a COPY of WP_Protocol under world/ with its
# __ExternalEntities__/WP_Protocol, _Landscape and _HLOD, cp -p, so the cook never writes into the repo):
#   build/Bin/Debug/WorldCook world/WP_Protocol.desce
#        --out world/WP_Protocol.dwworld --project Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --project-registry
#   build/Bin/Debug/DesertServer --project Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --role all
#        --world <scratch>/world/WP_Protocol.desce --source 0,0,0 --steps 600   > mesh0_mac_server.log
#   otool -L build/Bin/Debug/DesertServer                                     > mesh0_mac_server.otool.txt
# Тогда [mesh0_mac_server]: the log shows "no device created", the cooked index loaded with its cook hash, 600 steps
# at 60 Hz and the residency union of one source; the otool list names no Vulkan/MoltenVK/Metal/AppKit/Cocoa.
# Pass 3 (Тогда [mesh0_core_split]): DesertServer links the module Core (render-free, configure-checked) instead
# of a source list; the same run gives the same cook hash and 600 steps, otool -L > mesh0_core_split.otool.txt.
# Regression (here): the client still builds and opens WP_Protocol unchanged (ReadCookedWorld moved to CookedWorld).
# Pass 4 (Тогда [mesh0_linux_server]): the Linux server image, built by Server/Dockerfile (preset linux-server-clang,
# DESERT_SERVER_ONLY: no Vulkan SDK, no editor/player/tools) from a context with submodules dereferenced:
#   docker build --platform linux/amd64 -f Server/Dockerfile -t desert-server <context>
# Pass 5: the image comes from CI (job server-linux; optick/meshoptimizer fetched in the image at the commits
# ThirdParty/GitDependencies.json pins, scripts/FetchGitDependencies.py), not a local build:
#   gh run download <run> -n desert-server-image && gunzip -c desert-server.tar.gz | docker load
#   docker run --platform linux/amd64 -v <repo>/Projects/Desert:/project:ro -v <scratch>/world:/world
#        desert-server --project /project/Desert.deproj --role all --world /world/WP_Protocol.desce
#        --source 0,0,0 --steps 600                                            > mesh0_linux_server.log
#   docker run --platform linux/amd64 --entrypoint file desert-server /opt/desert/DesertServer >> the same log
# Pass 6: the job builds first-party code for the x86-64 baseline. A function using a newer instruction set than
# the target's minimum carries that set itself and runs behind a runtime CPU check (Crc32c.cpp Crc32cHardware,
# target("sse4.2") on clang/gcc). Checked before CI: every DesertServer TU compiled for -arch x86_64 -c.
#   gh workflow run ci.yml --ref task/NET-MESH-0; the run's desert-server-image is loaded and run as pass 5.
